# Every call that runs a method by a name it is handed lowers its file when
# the name is computed, not only `send` and `public_send`: `__send__`, `try`
# and `method` once came out clear. A literal name is a reference the index
# records, so it lowers nothing. A string names a method the index does not
# record: it lowers that method, not its file (Stringed#named came out clear). A send in a string of code
# (Evaluated) or behind a literal send of a send (Meta) once escaped the
# parse, and so did one through `.strip` (Stripped), which extraction reads.
# A string says so beside one call too: Inlined#named is no inlining
# candidate while `send("named")` reaches it.
dead app Underscored#small_attrs=unreferenced~__send__ Tried#small_attrs=unreferenced~try Handled#small_attrs=unreferenced~method Literal#unused=unreferenced~ Stringed#named=unreferenced~"named" Stringed#other=unreferenced~ Evaluated#small_attrs=unreferenced~public_send Meta#small_attrs=unreferenced~send Stripped#small_attrs=unreferenced~public_send Inlined#named=single-caller~"named"
